# two paths: only one is accepted, neither is read
$ skills lint <WORLD>/good/SKILL.md <WORLD>/bad/SKILL.md
exit: 1
--- stdout ---
--- stderr ---
error: skills lint: unexpected extra argument "<WORLD>/bad/SKILL.md" (lint accepts exactly one path)

# a second path after the flags of the wrapper
$ skills lint <WORLD>/good/SKILL.md --source-root <WORLD>/skills <WORLD>/bad/SKILL.md
exit: 1
--- stdout ---
--- stderr ---
error: skills lint: unexpected extra argument "<WORLD>/bad/SKILL.md" (lint accepts exactly one path)

# --rules and two paths: the second is refused before the rules are printed
$ skills lint --rules <WORLD>/good/SKILL.md <WORLD>/bad/SKILL.md
exit: 1
--- stdout ---
--- stderr ---
error: skills lint: unexpected extra argument "<WORLD>/bad/SKILL.md" (lint accepts exactly one path)

